{#
Agenda: a flat list, skipping empty days.

This is the pane's default view, and the reason the pane is useful at all — a
narrow column beside your mail should answer "what is coming up", not draw a
grid nobody can read at that width.

**The rail and the row are not here.** They live in
calendar/_agenda_shell.html.twig, which the public shared-calendar page embeds
too; what is left in this file is the chips that open an editor and the empty
state that offers to create one. The shell's header says why, and says why the
shared page prints its empty days when this one does not.
#}

{# The view's clock, not the reader's — see _view_month for why. #}
{% embed 'calendar/_agenda_shell.html.twig' with {
    dayKeys: days|keys,
    days:    days,
    today:   'now'|date('Y-m-d', range.zone),
} %}
    {% block day_entries %}
        <div class="space-y-0.5">
            {% for cluster in dayEntries %}
                {# The one view that prints a range rather than a start.
                   An agenda row draws no timeline, so "18:00" alone cannot
                   answer how long the meeting is; a grid block answers that by
                   being that tall, and a month cell has no width to spare. #}
                {% include 'calendar/_event_chip.html.twig' with { showRange: true } %}
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    {% endblock %}

    {% block empty_state %}
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-2 py-12 px-4 text-center text-ink-faint">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-calendar text-2xl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <p class="text-sm">{{ 'calendar.empty'|trans }}</p>
            <button type="button"
               data-controller="ui--modal"
               data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
               data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_calendar_event_new') }}"
               data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'calendar.event.new'|trans }}"
               class="text-sm text-accent hover:underline">
                {{ 'calendar.event.new'|trans }}
            </button>
        </div>
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
